    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE Announcement</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/announce/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/announce/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div id=&#34;preamble&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Date: December 2, 2025&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The FreeBSD Release Engineering Team is pleased to announce the availability of FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE.&#xA;This is the first release of the stable/15 branch.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Some of the highlights:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;ulist&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The FreeBSD &amp;#34;base&amp;#34; system can now be installed and managed using the pkg(8) package manager (see &amp;#34;Packaged base system&amp;#34; below).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The FreeBSD 15.0 release artifacts (install images, VM images, etc.) were all generated without requiring root privilege.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;FreeBSD now has a native inotify implementation, simplifying directory watching and software porting.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;OpenZFS has been upgraded to 2.4.0-rc4.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;OpenSSL has been upgraded to the latest long-term support (LTS) version, 3.5.4, which includes support for QUIC and now standardized quantum-resistant algorithms, ML-KEM, ML-DSA, and SLH-DSA.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;OpenSSH has been upgraded to 10.0p2 which includes support for quantum-resistant key agreement by default.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE EC2 AMIs</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/ec2-ami-ids/release/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/ec2-ami-ids/release/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_introduction&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This page lists EC2 AMIs for FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE.&#xA;You can filter the list of AMIs by region, architecture, flavour, and/or root filesystem.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Note that these are the original images from the release and do not have any post-release security or errata fixes; you may want the &lt;a href=&#34;../latest&#34;&gt;latest patched AMIs for FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE&lt;/a&gt; instead.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;These AMI IDs are available programmatically via the AWS SSM Parameter Store:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;literalblock&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;content&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;$ aws --region ${REGION} ssm get-parameter \&#xA;    --query &amp;#39;Parameter.Value&amp;#39; --output text \&#xA;    --name /aws/service/freebsd/${ARCH}/${FLAVOUR}/${FILESYSTEM}/15.0/RELEASE&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE EC2 Patched AMIs</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/ec2-ami-ids/latest/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/ec2-ami-ids/latest/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_introduction&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This page lists EC2 AMIs for FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE with the latest post-release security and errata fixes applied.&#xA;You can filter the list of AMIs by region, architecture, flavour, and/or root filesystem.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A separate page lists the &lt;a href=&#34;../release&#34;&gt;original images from the release&lt;/a&gt; without any post-release security and errata fixes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;These AMI IDs are available programmatically via the AWS SSM Parameter Store:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;literalblock&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;content&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;$ aws --region ${REGION} ssm get-parameter \&#xA;    --query &amp;#39;Parameter.Value&amp;#39; --output text \&#xA;    --name /aws/service/freebsd/${ARCH}/${FLAVOUR}/${FILESYSTEM}/15.0/RELEASE/latest&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE Errata</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/errata/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/errata/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_abstract&#34;&gt;Abstract&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This document lists errata items for FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE, containing significant information discovered after the release or too late in the release cycle to be otherwise included in the release documentation.&#xA;This information includes security advisories, as well as news relating to the software or documentation that could affect its operation or usability.&#xA;An up-to-date version of this document should always be consulted before installing this version of FreeBSD.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This errata document for FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE will be maintained until the release of FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE Installation Instructions</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/installation/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/installation/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_abstract&#34;&gt;Abstract&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This article gives some brief instructions on installing FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE and upgrading the systems running earlier releases.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_table_of_contents&#34;&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;ulist&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#install&#34;&gt;Installing FreeBSD&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#upgrade&#34;&gt;Upgrading FreeBSD&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;install&#34;&gt;Installing FreeBSD&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.freebsd.msk.ru/doc/en/books/handbook/bsdinstall/&#34;&gt;Installing FreeBSD&lt;/a&gt; chapter of the FreeBSD Handbook provides more in-depth information about the installation program itself, including a guided walk-through with screenshots.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;upgrade&#34;&gt;Upgrading FreeBSD&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you are upgrading from a previous release of FreeBSD, please read the upgrading section in the &lt;a href=&#34;../relnotes&#34;&gt;Release Notes&lt;/a&gt; for notable incompatibilities carefully.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE README</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/readme/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/readme/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_abstract&#34;&gt;Abstract&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This document gives a brief introduction to FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE.&#xA;It includes some information on how to obtain FreeBSD, a listing of various ways to contact the FreeBSD Project, and pointers to some other sources of information.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_table_of_contents&#34;&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;ulist&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#intro&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#obtain&#34;&gt;Obtaining FreeBSD&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#contacting&#34;&gt;Contacting the FreeBSD Project&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#seealso&#34;&gt;Further Reading&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#acknowledgements&#34;&gt;Acknowledgments&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;intro&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This distribution is a release of FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE, the latest point along the 15-STABLE branch.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;about&#34;&gt;About FreeBSD&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;FreeBSD is an open source operating system derived from 4.4 BSD Lite2 for 64-bit x86-based PC hardware (amd64), 64-bit Arm® ARMv8-A AArch64 systems (aarch64), 32-bit Arm® ARMv7 systems (armv7), 64-bit PowerPC® systems (powerpc64, powerpc64le), and 64-bit RISC-V (riscv64) systems.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE Release Notes</title>
      <link>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/relnotes/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.freebsd.org/releases/15.0R/relnotes/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;sect1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;_abstract&#34;&gt;Abstract&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;sectionbody&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;paragraph abstract-title&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The release notes for FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE contain a summary of the changes made to the FreeBSD base system on the 15-STABLE development line.&#xA;This document lists applicable security advisories that were issued since the last release, as well as significant changes to the FreeBSD kernel and userland.&#xA;Some brief remarks on upgrading are also presented.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;toc&#34; class=&#34;toc&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;toctitle&#34; class=&#34;title&#34;&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel1&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#_abstract&#34;&gt;Abstract&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#intro&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#upgrade&#34;&gt;Upgrading from Previous Releases of FreeBSD&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#upgrade-fu&#34;&gt;Upgrading from Distribution Sets&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#upgrade-rc&#34;&gt;Upgrading from Packages&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#upgrade-mk&#34;&gt;Upgrading from Source&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#security-errata&#34;&gt;Included Security Fixes and Errata Patches&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#security&#34;&gt;Fixed Security Advisories&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#errata&#34;&gt;Patched Errata Notices&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#architectures&#34;&gt;Architectures&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland&#34;&gt;Userland&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-config&#34;&gt;Userland Configuration Changes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-programs&#34;&gt;Userland Application Changes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-contrib&#34;&gt;Contributed Software&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-libraries&#34;&gt;Runtime Libraries and API&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-misc&#34;&gt;Miscellaneous&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#userland-deprecated-programs&#34;&gt;Deprecated Applications&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#cloud&#34;&gt;Cloud Support&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#kernel&#34;&gt;Kernel&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#kernel-general&#34;&gt;General Kernel Changes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#kernel-architecture-specific&#34;&gt;Architecture-Specific Changes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#drivers&#34;&gt;Devices and Drivers&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#drivers-device&#34;&gt;Device Drivers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#drivers-removals&#34;&gt;Deprecated and Removed Drivers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#storage&#34;&gt;Storage&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;sectlevel2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#storage-general&#34;&gt;General Storage&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#storage-nfs&#34;&gt;NFS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#storage-ufs&#34;&gt;UFS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#storage-zfs&#34;&gt;ZFS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#storage-geom&#34;&gt;GEOM&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#boot-loader&#